          "date": "2026-10-26 19:51:44.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-21038 lnet: add AF_XDP-style userspace socket interface",
        "message": "LU-21038 lnet: add AF_XDP-style userspace socket interface\n\nAdd /dev/lnsk, an LNet socket modelled on AF_XDP.  Each open of the\ndevice is one socket.  Userspace registers a pinned memory area (the\nUMEM, divided into chunks), creates fill, RX, TX and completion rings\nthat it mmap()s from the descriptor, and exchanges buffers with the\nkernel through them without copying data; the ioctls stand in for\nthe AF_XDP setsockopt(), bind() and sendto() calls.  Binding attaches\nthe socket to a portal: fill-ring chunks become single-use PUT target\nMDs, also answering GETs when bound with LNSK_BIND_GET, and a PUT\nreceived or GET answered is reported on the RX ring; TX-ring entries\nare bound as MDs and sent with LNetPut() or LNetGet(), and the final\nevent on each is reported on the completion ring with its status.  A\nring slot is reserved when an MD is posted, so the event handler\nnever finds a ring full.  poll() and LNSK_IOC_WAKEUP post the fill\nring and then send the TX ring; a work item reposts after receives.\n\nAdd lnsk_test, which exercises the interface over 0@lo, sanity-lnet\ntest_700 (PUT) and test_701 (GET) running it.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I0c1f586b38f656f03be84d6f67aa142b6a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
